 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Similar to standard 3DGS rasterization, as the masking operation is a simple multiplication per splat per pixel. The overhead is negligible.
-- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing an additional mask value per Gaussian.
+- **Time Complexity:** Similar to standard 3DGS rasterization, as the masking operation is a simple multiplication per splat per pixel. The overhead is negligible [G].
+- **Memory Complexity:** Requires storing an additional mask value per Gaussian [S1].
 - **Performance:** Achieves pruning ratios of 62.4% (Mip-NeRF360), 67.7% (Tanks & Temples), and 75.3% (Deep Blending) with speedups of 2.05×, 2.19×, and 3.16× respectively, with only a 0.02 PSNR decline on the first two datasets [S1].
-- **Strengths:** Prevents "stale" Gaussians from becoming outdated by allowing them to receive gradients for their existence probability. Superior to multiplying masks with opacity/scale.
-- **Limitations:** Requires careful implementation to ensure gradients do not flow to geometric attributes for masked Gaussians.
