 ## Background
-Masked-Rasterization was introduced in the **MaskGaussian** paper by researchers at Shanghai AI Laboratory, presented at CVPR 2025 [S1]. It addresses the limitations of previous pruning methods (e.g., [4, 17, 34]) that multiplied masks with Gaussian attributes, which caused zero alpha filtering and blocked gradient flow. The method models Gaussians as probabilistic entities, allowing for dynamic assessment of their contribution to the evolving scene.
